Task 2: Shape modeling with circles
ENG
The user must be able to place circles on the screen using mouse clicks (by selecting the center point
followed by the radius). A tube-like shape must be generated using the circles in the order they were
placed; one possible method for this is to create an "envelope" around the circles, as discussed in the
lecture. To achieve this, we must determine where the shape should touch the circles and identify the
tangent vectors at those points; then, using this information, we can calculate a local Hermite curve
for each pair of points and tangent vectors.
Another option is to use a Ball-Bézier or Disk-Bézier curve, where the placed circles function as "control
circles." The curve itself is a Bézier curve defined by the circle centers as control points, but with a
thickness calculated from the radii in a manner similar to the curve itself.
Ideally, the team should implement both methods (teams of one need only implement one).